        "answer": {
          "short": "\\$75 and \\$45; both methods give the same shares.",
          "worked": "Unitary method:\n$$\\begin{align*}5+3&=8\\text{ parts}\\\\1\\text{ part}&=\\$120\\div8=\\$15\\\\5\\text{ parts}&=5\\times\\$15=\\$75\\\\3\\text{ parts}&=3\\times\\$15=\\$45\\end{align*}$$\nFraction method:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{5}{8}\\times\\$120&=\\$75\\\\\\frac{3}{8}\\times\\$120&=\\$45\\end{align*}$$\nBoth methods give \\$75 and \\$45, so Olivia is correct.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
